WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:08.150
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:14.660
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.490
It's my day!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.070
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.480
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:41.850
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.260
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.030
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:02.170
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.680
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.820
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.890
I just want to walk

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.420
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.400
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:35.300
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:41.740
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.010
It's my day!

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.100
Tsukushi Makino

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.110
A weed will always survive,
wherever it goes.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.850
<i>That's what I decided.</i>

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.780
<i>But it's still hard to believe...</i>

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.130
<i>Maybe I was just seeing things...</i>

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.000
<i>Maybe in my head,
I wish I was seeing things...</i>

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:50.820
"Our New Relationship"

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.520
It must be a joke!

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.290
Who'd have thought
Makino would pass?!

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.860
I don't believe it!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.330
Good job, Tsukushi!

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.190
Tsukushi.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.830
Makino. You didn't cheat, did you?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.830
I bet she did.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.450
Tsukushi isn't like that!

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.240
If you bad-mouth Tsukushi,
I won't forgive you!

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.740
My, what a pair you make!

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.250
Don't do it. 
You'll catch their rottenness.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.680
Hey! You two...

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.520
Look! Domyoji and his group
are coming this way!

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.860
Wow! Makino actually passed!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:43.870
Tsukushi Makino

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.280
Makino sure has willpower.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.210
She really is something,
to pass that exam.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.210
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.150
Tsukushi Makino

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.850
<i>It wasn't my imagination.</i>

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.130
Tsukushi!

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.400
Congratulations, Tsukushi!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.330
You did it, didn't you?!

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.000
Thanks, everybody...

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.310
Nice job, Tsukushi.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.780
To be honest,
I'm just as surprised as you.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:06.780
But if you go away,
it'll be pretty lonely around here.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:07.850
Yeah...

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:10.820
<i>Kazuya...</i>

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.460
<i>Makiko...</i>

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.720
Aw, come on! It's not as though
we'll never see her again.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.700
Let's not get so emotional.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.670
That's right. I'll write letters.
And there's always the phone, right?

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.810
I won't forget about you all!

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.650
Really? Promise, now...

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.550
I'll be rooting for you
no matter where you are.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:35.680
Me, too.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.680
Thanks. I'll do my best.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.590
<i>It'll be good-bye
to this garden, soon...</i>

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.410
<i>I want you to come back.</i>

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.460
<i>I won't run away again.</i>

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.880
<i>Rui Hanazawa can hear
the voice of the violin, once more.</i>

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:13.950
<i>And I...</i>

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:17.380
<i>I can change now.</i>

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.290
<i>Why not? It was the truth.</i>

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.190
<i>It may be the truth,
but some things shouldn't be told.</i>

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.100
<i>You like to stuff everything
inside of you like that, huh?</i>

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.740
<i>Why don't you just be honest, for once?</i>

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.180
<i>I may not be able to be honest,</i>

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.650
<i>but I might be able
to find something else.</i>

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:57.790
Shigeru...

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.860
Are you really going?

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.360
I transferred here
because you were here.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.530
It'll be no fun if you leave.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.400
Forget the exchange program
and stay here... Please!

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:17.040
I'm sorry. I've made my decision.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.450
Take good care of Domyoji.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:22.480
Tsukushi!

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.620
<i>I don't know
what Shigeru is up to...</i>

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.450
<i>but I can't stay here.</i>

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:33.420
<i>For her sake... and for mine...</i>

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.200
Tsukushi...

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.500
You're a very interesting person.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:51.480
You're Shigeru Okawahara, aren't you?

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:57.450
Makino is your rival in love...

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.590
so why would you try
to keep her here?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.420
Well...

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:09.460
If you feel like talking,
come to the nurse's office.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.600
I might be able to help you out.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:29.710
Tsukushi Makino

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.920
So, poor li'l Tsukushi's
going on the exchange program?

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:37.790
<i>Domyoji...</i>

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.430
Guess we should always
excite the unexcited.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:42.460
Huh?!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.460
Don't you mean,
"expect the unexpected?"

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.500
Your speech is as poor as ever.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.010
Why, you...!

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:56.370
If I were you, I'd hit the books!
In one year, <i>I</i> will be bilingual.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.280
Bilingual?
Don't you mean "bisexual"?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.120
Bisexual?! How dare you!

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:30.110
You really did it, didn't you?
You actually passed...

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.180
<i>Domyoji...</i>

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:47.990
Bye-bye, Domyoji.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.260
Makino!

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.460
<i>I mustn't look back again.</i>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.630
<i>I must only think
about going forward!</i>

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.800
<i>Bisexual?! How dare you!</i>

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:17.980
<i>Bye-bye, Domyoji.</i>

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.940
That obstacle will be
out of the way for a while.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:45.080
With Makino Tsukushi out of the picture,
Tsukasa's feelings for her should fade.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:50.080
Meanwhile, I'd better firm up
our agreement with the Okawaharas.

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:56.390
So, <i>that's</i> your game!
It was nothing but a dirty trick!

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:58.590
Damn you, you witch! Go to hell!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:04.000
How dare you speak to me like that!
You are the Domyoji heir!

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:08.200
Is it any wonder you still need
your mother to look after you?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.780
You were never around
when I was little.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:13.740
When you finally bother to come home,
you mess up my life!

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.940
I don't consider you my mother!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.360
Tsukasa!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:22.750
Why do you think you're able
to live a free and easy life?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.350
Because you are a member 
of this Domyoji family!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.890
I didn't ask to be born 
into this rotten family!

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.260
Tsukasa!

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.260
Master!

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.000
<i>What? Really?</i>

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.480
Yeah. It's so unexpected.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.060
<i>Hello? Tsukushi...?</i>

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.940
Uh, it's nothing... I won't be leaving
for a while, anyway.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.040
But it's amazing... When you get there,
you'll have to speak English, right?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.550
You'll be fluent
by the time you return!

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:30.980
I sure hope so!

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.230
<i>Maybe you'll get yourself
an American boyfriend.</i>

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.150
Knock it off, Yuki!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.790
But maybe I will.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:05.050
<i>I've told my folks and Yuki...
It's beginning to feel real.</i>

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:17.700
<i>Tsukushi!</i>

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:21.400
<i>What do you think?</i>

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.700
<i>A different color
really makes a difference.</i>

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.770
<i>I'm back!
I picked up some riceballs.</i>

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.860
<i>And soon,
I have to say good-bye...</i>

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.950
<i>...to this apartment
that we all redecorated...</i>

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:41.590
<i>Okay. But I'm through
being sentimental!</i>

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.690
What'll happen
after my year away?

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.090
Lots of wonderful things,
I'll bet!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.600
"Trouble Ahead"?!

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:08.250
No way!

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:13.300
I, Tsukushi Makino,
swear to become bilingual...

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.690
...and to find
a nice American boyfriend!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.660
Who's making all that noise?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.430
Makino! Makino!
You're there, aren't you?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:28.770
Makino!

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:29.830
Domyoji...

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:35.010
Be quiet! The neighbors will...

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.610
W-wait, Domyoji...

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:42.370
I didn't say you could come in!

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.280
Don't go!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.280
Don't go on the
exchange program!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.090
Huh? What do you mean?

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.960
My mother.
She was behind all of this.

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:57.100
It was a scheme
to get you away from me.

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:08.340
I knew it... I thought it was weird.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.540
There was no way
I could have passed...

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.880
Don't go anywhere.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:25.820
I <i>will</i> go!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:34.400
It doesn't feel right knowing
I didn't qualify on my own,

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:37.100
but if I stay here,
nothing will change.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.740
I want to change.
That's why I'm going.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.340
No, you fool! Don't you see?

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.510
I don't want you to go!

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:51.480
What are you saying, Domyoji?
You have Shigeru!

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.850
There's nothing between us.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:56.550
<i>Shigeru!</i>

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.160
You're lying!
What about Shigeru's villa...

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.930
I told her clearly.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.170
That she wasn't the one.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.170
<i>You make me so mad!
Say what you mean!</i>

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:15.910
<i>You're not the one.</i>

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:21.080
That made her really mad.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:34.690
I don't blame her.
I hurt her very badly.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:36.790
I don't understand...

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:41.130
Then why did Shigeru
transfer to Eitoku?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.870
I don't understand either,
what she's up to.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.870
But what I do know is...

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:53.480
You're the only one for me.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.640
<i>Domyoji...</i>

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.870
<i>Domyoji still loves me?</i>

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:34.990
<i>But... still... in my heart...</i>

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.130
Domyoji.

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:47.900
I don't have the confidence
to live in your world.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:52.370
Even if I did love you...

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.540
I told you once.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:00.910
I follow you
to the ends of the earth.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:07.350
If you won't come,
I'll leap into your world.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:16.660
Domyoji?

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:21.130
Besides, your mom's stewed potatoes
are pretty good.

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.300
<i>Stewed potatoes?!</i>

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:26.200
Domyoji, you can't just...

00:20:56.130 --> 00:21:00.100
<i>For Domyoji
to leap into my world...</i>

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:04.840
<i>It wouldn't be easy at all.</i>

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:09.850
<i>But I can believe him for now...</i>

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.470
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.350
<i>Our new relationship.</i>

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:04.280
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:09.030
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:18.500
Some day, the whole world

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:24.310
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:32.060
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:37.680
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:44.300
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:50.700
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:57.600
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:06.480
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:14.390
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:20.450
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:27.710
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:31.100
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:36.970
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:47.540
I went to see Domyoji
at his home.

00:23:47.870 --> 00:23:50.940
Waiting for me there was...
Kaede Domyoji...

00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:53.210
The way you think is too selfish.

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:56.210
Now, I can understand
how he feels.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:00.320
I want to see you.
Come out, Domyoji!

00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:04.620
Hana Yori Dango: 
"Time To Call It Quits"

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:07.830
Thanks, Domyoji...
